  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1254 PM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nSaturday will end up being one of the warmer days of the extended \nforecast as an upper low approaches from the west. Highs jump \ninto the 70s for most with winds increasing out of the west. A \ncold front is pushed through Saturday night as the upper low moves\ninto the Plains. Highs on Sunday will only make it into the 50s \nfor most. High pressure takes over to begin next week and into \nearly December. Highs in the 60s and 70s, around 5-10 degrees \nabove normal for this time of year, are forecast through at least \nthe middle of the week. Long range guidance continues to keep \nprecipitation chances near zero through at least Tuesday before \nlow(10-30%) chances appear Wednesday into Thursday next week. \n\n-Stickney",
